{
  "id": "ethylene_gas___specific_heat_vs__temperature",
  "title": "Ethylene Gas - Specific Heat vs. Temperature",
  "description": "Specific heat of Ethylene Gas - C2H4 - temperatures ranging 175 - 900 K. This tool allows you to view and interpolate specific heat values at different temperatures.",
  "type": "calculator-chart",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Ethylene Gas - Specific Heat vs. Temperature\n\n**Specific heat (C)** is the amount of heat required to _change the temperature of a mass unit of a substance by one degree._\n\n- **Isobaric specific heat (Cp)** is used for substances in a _constant pressure_ (ΔP = 0) system.\n- **Isochoric specific heat (Cv)** is used for substances in a _constant-volume_, (= _isovolumetric_ or _isometric_) closed system.\n\nThe specific heat will vary with temperature. This tool provides data for Ethylene (C2H4) at gas-liquid equilibrium pressure with temperatures ranging from 175 K to 900 K."
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "temperature",
          "label": "Temperature",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "K",
          "defaultValue": 300
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "specific_heat",
          "label": "Specific Heat (cp)",
          "unit": "kJ/kgK",
          "format": "decimal",
          "formula": "1.295 + (inputs.temperature - 175) * (3.180 - 1.295) / (900 - 175)"
        }
      ]
    },
